BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Ralph E. Cheek
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
DTSTAMP:20260830T224458Z
UID:wrightfuneralhomeobit-2026-08-25-ralph-e-cheek-2026-08-25-allday@linn-
 county-scraper.local
CATEGORIES:obituary
DESCRIPTION:Ralph E. Cheek\, age 58\, of Bucklin\, passed away Tuesday\, A
 ugust 25\, 2026\, at his home. Ralph was a simple man who enjoyed spending
  his time at home and doing the things he loved. He was always tinkering w
 ith something and especially enjoyed working on his motorcycle. Although h
 e was a homebody at heart\, Ralph appreciated the friendships he shared wi
 th his neighbors and those in the Bucklin community. Family held a special
  place in Ralph’s heart. Although he never had children of his own\, he 
 loved his nieces and nephews as though they were his own. He shared a uniq
 ue relationship with each of them and was known for giving several of them
  special nicknames that became a cherished part of their memories with him
 . Even though distance often separated Ralph from many members of his fami
 ly\, it never diminished the love they shared. He was deeply loved and wil
 l be remembered for the special place he held within his family. His prese
 nce\, his personality\, and the memories they made together will be greatl
 y missed. Ralph is survived by his sister\, Paula Holden of Athens\, Alaba
 ma\; 11 nieces and nephews\, Tathamber Corum and husband\, Kevin\, Brittan
 y Beadle and husband\, Brandon\, Brett Beadle and wife\, Katherine\, Kevin
  Neely\, Thomas Neely\, Anthony Cruppi\, Heavenly Cruppi\, Katlyn Cruppi\,
  Keanu Salguero\, Ashlee Salguero\, and Tyler Salguero\; and eight great-n
 ieces and great-nephews\, Goob Beadle\, Clayton Pugh\, Hayley Corum\, Gann
 on McBay\, Peanut Beadle\, Heifer Crosslin\, Millie Beadle\, and Maci Salg
 uero. Memorials contributions to Wright Funeral Home ( to be used toward f
 uneral expenses)\, may be left at or mailed to Wright Funeral Home\, P.O. 
 Box\, 496\, Brookfield\, MO 64628.\n\nFull obituary and service details: h
 ttps://www.wright-funeralhome.com/obituaries/Ralph-E-Cheek?obId=49384444
LOCATION:Bucklin\, MO
X-EVENT-TYPE:Obituary / Visitation
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Kathy Hunt
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260821
DTSTAMP:20260830T224458Z
UID:wrightfuneralhomeobit-2026-08-20-kathy-hunt-2026-08-20-allday@linn-cou
 nty-scraper.local
CATEGORIES:obituary
DESCRIPTION:Kathy Hunt\, age 80\, of Meadville\, passed away peacefully on
  Thursday\, August 20\, 2026\, at Pershing Memorial Hospital in Brookfield
 . Mary Kathleen\, daughter of Woody Templeman and Claudia (Dawkins) Dulane
 y\, was born December 8\, 1945\, in Chillicothe. On December 5\, 1986\, sh
 e married Kenny Hunt\, with whom she shared nearly 40 years of marriage. K
 athy was a 1963 graduate of Meadville High School. Throughout her working 
 years\, she built a career in administrative work\, spending the majority 
 of those years with the Bank of Brookfield-Purdin\, where she worked in bo
 th the Meadville and Brookfield locations. She is survived by her husband
 \, Kenny Hunt of the home\; two daughters\, Theresa Triplett and husband\,
  Tom\, of Linneus\, and Holly Gasper and fiancé\, Matt Englert\, of Meadv
 ille\; one son\, Paul Chapman Jr. of Osage\, MO\; one stepson\, Kenneth Ja
 mes Hunt of Moberly\; eight grandchildren\, Jessica Young\, Sarah Samenus
 \, Wayne Triplett\, Alan Gasper\, Jonathon Gasper\, Waylon Chapman\, Skyla
 r Chapman\, and Chevelle Chapman\; several great-grandchildren\; one broth
 er\, Mike Templeman of Brookfield\; three sisters\, Mary Ann Scott of Chil
 licothe\, Cindy Walsh and husband\, Roger\, of Brookfield\, and Marylyn Ev
 ans and husband\, David\, of Laclede\; as well as several nieces\, nephews
 \, and other relatives. Kathy was preceded in death by her father\, Woody 
 Templeman\; her mother and stepfather\, Claudia and Bill Dulaney\; her sis
 ter-in-law\, Linda Templeman\; and her brother-in-law\, Alan Scott. In acc
 ordance with Kathy’s wishes\, cremation will take place and no services 
 will be held. Her family and friends will remember her privately\, holding
  close the memories of the years they were fortunate to share with her.\n
 \nFull obituary and service details: https://www.wright-funeralhome.com/ob
 ituaries/Kathy-Hunt?obId=49332019
LOCATION:Brookfield\, MO
X-EVENT-TYPE:Obituary / Visitation
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Patsy Lou Asher
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
DTSTAMP:20260830T224458Z
UID:wrightfuneralhomeobit-2026-08-10-patsy-lou-asher-2026-08-10-allday@lin
 n-county-scraper.local
CATEGORIES:obituary
DESCRIPTION:Patsy Lou Asher\, age 89\, of Brookfield\, passed away Monday
 \, August 10\, 2026\, at Pershing Memorial Hospital in Brookfield. A Celeb
 ration of Patsy’s life will be held Thursday\, August 20\, 2026\, at 2:0
 0 p.m. at Wright Funeral Home in Brookfield with Bro. Jeremy Blackburn off
 iciating.  Burial will take place at Park Lawn Cemetery in Brookfield. The
  family will receive friends from 1:00 p.m. until the time of service at t
 he funeral home. Memorials to Pershing Memorial Auxiliary may be left at o
 r mailed to Wright Funeral Home\, P.O. Box 496\, Brookfield\, MO 64628. Pa
 tsy was born August 27\, 1936\, in Brookfield\, the daughter of Raymond Mo
 rris and Bessie Mae (Adams) Sims. She was a graduate of Brookfield High Sc
 hool. On September 26\, 1954\, she married Donald B. Asher who preceded he
 r in death on August 5\, 1980. A familiar face to many throughout the Broo
 kfield community\, Patsy worked for many years as a salesclerk at longtime
  local businesses\, including Tooey's and Mart Drug\, as well as several o
 ther retail businesses in the area. Through her work\, she came to know co
 untless people and enjoyed the friendships she made along the way. Patsy w
 as also a talented seamstress whose abilities were well known throughout t
 he Brookfield area. Over the years\, she sewed for many people in the comm
 unity and generously shared her talents with others. One especially meanin
 gful part of her work was ordering and fitting prosthesis and bras for bre
 ast cancer survivors\, providing a service that brought comfort and confid
 ence to many women. Outside of work\, Patsy had a great passion for playin
 g golf and enjoyed staying active through water aerobics. She also looked 
 forward to attending Ray Ball Auction with her friends\, where she enjoyed
  the company\, conversation\, and time spent together.  Above all else\, 
 Patsy's greatest joy was her family. She dearly loved her children\, grand
 children\, and great-grandchildren and was always proud to share a story a
 bout them. Her family was never far from her thoughts or conversations\, a
 nd the memories and stories she shared will remain a treasured part of her
  legacy. Patsy is survived by her companion\, Terry Kenley of the home\; t
 wo sons\, Donald Asher and wife\, Brenda\, of Brookfield\, and Mark Asher 
 of Lee's Summit\; six grandchildren\, Bailey Calton and husband\, Dave\, o
 f Lawson\, Kirby Asher and wife\, Kellie\, of Harrisburg\, Brandon Asher a
 nd wife\, Kellan\, of Oak Park\, California\, Aaron Asher and wife\, Jessi
 ca\, of Greenwood\, Tyler Asher and wife\, Amanda\, of Lee's Summit\, and 
 Trevor Asher and wife\, Abby\, of Lee's Summit\; 13 great-grandchildren\; 
 a sister-in-law\, Sylvia Morris of St. Catharine\; brother-in-law and sist
 er-in-law Jim and Sheila Cook of Chillicothe\; and many nieces\, nephews\,
  and other relatives. She was also preceded in death by her parents\, Raym
 ond Morris and Bessie (Adams) Sims\; her stepfather\, Banty Sims\; two bro
 thers\, Johnny Morris and Ronald Morris\; a daughter-in-law\, Teresa "Terr
 i" Asher\; father-in-law and mother-in-law\, Ted and Viola Asher\;  sister
 s-in-law and brothers-in-law\, Shirley Asher Bohannon Cook\, Eldon Bohanno
 n\, and Ronald and Verna Asher. Patsy will be remembered for her independe
 nt spirit\, the many talents she shared with her community\, the friendshi
 ps she made throughout her life\, and\, most importantly\, the tremendous 
 love and pride she had for her family.\n\nFull obituary and service detail
 s: https://www.wright-funeralhome.com/obituaries/Patsy-Lou-Asher?obId=4922
 7949
LOCATION:Brookfield\, MO
X-EVENT-TYPE:Obituary / Visitation
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Dennis Ray Wright
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTSTAMP:20260830T224458Z
UID:delaneyfuneralhomeobit-2026-08-16-dennis-ray-wright-2026-08-16-allday@
 linn-county-scraper.local
CATEGORIES:obituary
DESCRIPTION:Dennis Ray Wright\, age 79\, of Marceline\, Missouri\, passed 
 away Sunday\, August 16\, 2026\, at Pioneer Skilled Nursing in Marceline. 
 Dennis was born on August 5\, 1947\, on the family farm in Chariton County
 \, Missouri\, the son of Carl Warren and Freda Louise (York) Wright. Denni
 s served in the United States Army and was united in marriage to Kathy Wes
 tfall on May 20\, 1967\, at St. Bonaventure Catholic Church in Marceline. 
 Dennis earned his Master’s degree from Missouri State Teachers College i
 n Kirksville\, Missouri. He worked as a guidance counselor at Macon Vo-Tec
 h. Teacher and coach at Marceline. After retiring\, he worked at Bucklin R
 -2 as a counselor. Dennis enjoyed farming\, hunting\, fishing\, and especi
 ally spending time with his family. Dennis is survived by his wife\, Kathy
 \, of Marceline\; three children\, Julie Lucas and her husband Randy\, Tho
 mas Wright\, and Alicen Wright\, all of Marceline\; six grandchildren\, Cl
 ayton\, Blake\, Whitney\, Winston\, Hillary\, and Justin\; seven great-gra
 ndchildren\, Bentley\, Zane\, Sally\, Remi\, Cooper\, Theodor\, and Emmy\;
  two brothers\, Rodney Wright and wife Shirley of Marceline and Lanny Wrig
 ht and wife Brenda of Chillicothe\; and one sister\, Mary James and husban
 d Ed of Calhoun\, Missouri. He was preceded in death by his parents and fo
 ur brothers\, Taylor\, Gerald “Abe\,” Allen\, and Bradly Wright. Arran
 gements are under the direction of Delaney Funeral Home in Marceline.\n\nF
 ull obituary and service details: https://www.delaneyfuneralhome.com/obitu
 aries/Dennis-Ray-Wright?obId=49298351
LOCATION:Marceline\, MO
X-EVENT-TYPE:Obituary / Visitation
END:VEVENT
